## Step 3 — Update research index

Edit `tools/_claude/research-index.md`:
1. Add a row to the appropriate category table (Metadata, Compute, Orchestration, etc.)
2. If the service was on the Todo list, mark it `[x]`

If a new repo was cloned during research (the coordinator will flag this), add a row to `tools/_claude/cloned-repos.md`.

---

## Step 4 — Git commit

```bash
cd /Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base
git add tools/<service>/
git add tools/_claude/research-index.md
git add tools/_claude/cloned-repos.md   # only if updated
git commit -m "<service>: initial research"
```

If this is an update to existing docs, use:
```bash
git commit -m "<service>: research update — <brief description of what changed>"
```

---

## Step 5 — Confirm to coordinator

Reply with:
- What files were written (with full paths)
- The git commit hash
- Any fields that had to be set to `"unknown"` (so the coordinator can surface them to the user)
- Any conflicts found between new research and existing docs (don't silently overwrite — note conflicts in CLAUDE.md open questions AND flag them in your reply)

---

## Rules

- Never invent data — if a field is missing from the coordinator's synthesis, use `"unknown"` or `"N/A"`
- If the service is already `Complete` in the index, do NOT overwrite existing docs — append new findings as a `## Update — <date>` section and update the index entry's last-updated date
- Follow the category definitions in `research-workflow.md` exactly — do not create new categories
- Check `org-naming-drift.md` if team names seem inconsistent before writing the `team:` field
